{"text": "Int Arch Occup Environ Health (1989) 61:519-525\n\nGeeupational~\nEnvironmental\n\nDust exposure, eye redness, eye cytology\nand mucous membrane irritation in a tobacco industry\n\nSoren K. Kjergaard and Ole F. Pedersen\n\nInsttate of Environmental and Occupational Medicine, University of Aarhus, Bygning 180, Universitetsparken,\n\n\u2018Dx-\u20ac000 Arbus C, Denmark\n\nsummary a study of75 workers employed in a to-\n\u2018bacco factory producing cheroots we measured cellu-\niar contents of tear fud, redness of eyes, discomfort,\ntotal (0-5.7 mg/m\u2019) and respirable dust in the brea-\n{hing 2oee and total ambient dust by stationary sam-\n\u2018pling (0.08-1.0me/m?), A matched group of 50 office\n\u2018rocker ina telephone company (total ambient dust\nconcentration between 0.08-0.13 mg/m\u201d) was simi-\nlary examined as referents, We found a diference\nbetween the two companies with regard. cell counts,\nwrth tobacco workers having the largest numbers\nxcept for lymphocytes. Among tobacco workers\ntte forbermore found thatthe number of cuboidal\nand, columnar epithelial cells increased during the\nday} The increase of cuboidal cel, however, 0c\naried mainly in a small group of tobacco workers\n\u2018exposed to the highest, trations of tobacco dust\n(mean = 1.26 mg/m\u2019). [No difference in the sensation\nof eye initation was found between companies, but\n\u2018nereased irritation in the morning was associated\nwith increased exposure to total dust during the work\nShit among tobacco workers. A dose-dependent di\nferenee in photographically measured eye redness\nwas found among the tobacco workers. It could not\nbe explained by differences in taco smoking, sex.\nage, sleeping abit or ute of lates. Iritaton of ips\nand upper airways as reported by questionaire were\ntore common i tobacco workers than in referents.\nIn conclusion the tobacco workers, more often than\nthe referents, had complaints and objective changes\nin the mucous membranes ofthe eyes. These may be\nrelated to tobacco dust expose]\n\nOffprint requests to: 8K. Kiergaacd\n\nKey words: Red eyes ~ Tear fluid ~ Polymorphonuc-\nlear leukocytes ~ Conjunctiva ~ Epithelium\n\nIntroduction\n\n\u2018The harmful effects of exposure to tobacco dust have\nonly been examined in afew studies (Valic etl. 1976;\n\u2018Cyetanov et al. 1982). These studies dealt with tobacco\n\u2018dust concentrations in the range of 1 to 31mg/m\u2019.\n\u2018They focused mainly on changes in lung function. A\nsmall Danish study has, however, also indicated icri-\ntative effects on the eyes (Lander 1986).\nSkin, nose and eye irritation as well as eyelid der-\n\u2018matits have been reported in individual eases (Rycroft\n1980), Short-term acute reaction in the nose during.\nthe first days or weeks of occupation has been reported\n1s a common experience (Hunter 1975).\n\u201cThe aim of this study was to demonstrate differ-\n\u2018ences between tobacco workers and a reference popu-\nlation with regard to changes in sensation of eye irri-\ntation, objective measurements of eye redness, and\ntear fluid composition, and also to try to establish\nrelationships between tobacco dust exposure in the\nbreathing zone on the one hand and symptoms and\nsigns on the other.\n\nMaterial and methods\n\nWorkers (n=231) were invited from atobaco factory produ:\ning cberoots, ie. a special form of sal cigars. Among these,\n136 (RE) agreed to participate. Of these, 94 were accepted\n\u2018ecoring to our inclusion entra, Le. more than one year of\n\u2018Employment. an &h working day, and daly exposure to to-\n\nsponte\n\nSbSTbESzOz",
